{"title":"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_-_Guessing_those_Squares\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 - Guessing those Squares</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Ambiguity,_Sanity_Checks)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Ambiguity, Sanity Checks)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Sidenote\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Sidenote</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Forty slips of paper numbered <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> are placed in a hat. Alice and Bob each draw one number from the hat without replacement, keeping their numbers hidden from each other. Alice says, \"I can't tell who has the larger number.\" Then Bob says, \"I know who has the larger number.\" Alice says, \"You do? Is your number prime?\" Bob replies, \"Yes.\" Alice says, \"In that case, if I multiply your number by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> and add my number, the result is a perfect square. \" What is the sum of the two numbers drawn from the hat?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/7/c973f6908cca55645f7c5989828c34f3dd985997.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }27\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }37\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }47\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }57\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }67$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"401\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let Alice have the number A, Bob B.\nWhen Alice says that she can't tell who has the larger number, it means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> cannot equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, it makes sense that Bob has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because he now knows that Alice has the larger number. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is also prime. The last statement means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/0/c00d5e80acd170a59f9eb373d4d0623bb8482a1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200+A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"65\" height=\"16\" /> is a perfect square. The three squares in the range <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/1/b71c28648779e5c778005c01134510a7ee453ddb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200-300$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"79\" height=\"15\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/1/5219cede5456639177ac2c4878419988f1867278.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$225$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/d/abd678361b0f40ec2723283c0f2bab3df5cadc68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$256$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/2/9a2815ecb054fadd5031fb990e85e4ec26a00879.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$289$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> could equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/9/6392be3c4d257afbc7ed9283bdb8ba630f4ef7e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$56$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/0/e609f93104b193a2355181ca62ff083ea9fd3821.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$89$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/3/b831312585cb4ab6697896f86b72accbddbc4b45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A+B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/5/1051e7d41ec0b8bd688a872be17538413f4ee97b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/8/b784ad3135944214ca7ecade87b8dfa3aa54f1f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$58$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/d/7fd34ff50f8bba26a08bc96a69e921daa60f5f12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$91$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, of only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/4/2e4fa04216675212d028a47682226b43db0d340e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }27}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"67\" height=\"30\" /> is below <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, therefore it is the correct answer since the maximum number one can have is 40.\n</p><p>--stjwyl\n</p><p>Minor edit ~SIGMAMATHEMATICIAN\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Denote by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> the numbers drawn by Alice and Bob, respectively.\n</p><p>Alice's sentence “I can't tell who has the larger number.” implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/c/c0ca7dddadfecce7df537ec580ad8333c18d703f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A \\in \\left\\{ 2 , \\cdots , 39 \\right\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"127\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Bob's sentence “I know who has the larger number.” implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/f/80f7b093f802d6b37eaa413117c92585e504b383.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B \\in \\left\\{ 1 , 2 , 39, 40 \\right\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"136\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Their subsequent conversation that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is prime implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/4/ed45766ae06d282b582b4b49d4289dcc81331314.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = 2$\" width=\"47\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>Then, Alice's next sentence  “In that case, if I multiply your number by 100 and add my number, the result is a perfect square.” implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/9/ed9b4ba7725bf8c421012d60cbb08e42afa104a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200 + A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"65\" height=\"16\" /> is a perfect square.\nHence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/4/134fb430e83f3aa1a44754db8599788ed2a28ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = 25$\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/4/2e4fa04216675212d028a47682226b43db0d340e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }27}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"67\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_-_Guessing_those_Squares\">Solution 3 - Guessing those Squares</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 - Guessing those Squares\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/1/5219cede5456639177ac2c4878419988f1867278.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$225$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> is one such square that works. Bob gets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and Alice gets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> which is valid. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/a/0bafd1e8e49c506297d38f285dde02b3fb6f61b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 25 = 27.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"99\" height=\"15\" /> So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/4/2e4fa04216675212d028a47682226b43db0d340e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }27}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"67\" height=\"30\" /> is our answer.\n</p><p>-D1r\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Ambiguity.2C_Sanity_Checks.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Ambiguity,_Sanity_Checks)\">Solution 4 (Ambiguity, Sanity Checks)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Ambiguity, Sanity Checks)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The MAA knows this problem is ambiguous, as the interpretation of what might be viewed as the \"middle\" of the set could be different for all. Then, they would have specifically designed the answer choices such that one choice is guaranteed to be correct while all others are unobtainable. \n</p><p>So, for a sanity check and our general satisfaction, we will use the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/6/61641bb403cb3ff3d595efdd1209f1f62a99b993.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{A} \\in \\{5,6,7,\\dots,34,35 \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"185\" height=\"20\" /> as all the possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/7/0b7bf42db84e4d2dbb7bf55476c12bf9f6233bc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/9/e89084defb5a19636fcd0a2d63f5ea113b82c6f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{B} \\in \\{1,2,3,4,36,37,38,39,40 \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"247\" height=\"20\" />. Alice notes that Bob's number is prime. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/8/a486dd7f9e12b49353d0ed1ca4787b44caa42abc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{B} \\in \\{2,3,4,37\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"124\" height=\"20\" />. Now, say Alice's number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. Then, each of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/0/c00d5e80acd170a59f9eb373d4d0623bb8482a1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200+A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"65\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/c/afcd807073c91d90b6439a6f6be4612257871824.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$300+A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"65\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/2/e6259cd9436c7910cb92e32be5a081168bc1f986.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3700+A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"16\" /> is prime. Note that in each case, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/e/38e2534ba0420f54fb5afd6f5841369d3d446d38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = 25, 24, 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"18\" /> respectively. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/7/317b1fc80e6eb29ce317b5140ccd578fc9f75193.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A+B = 27, 27, 58$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"147\" height=\"18\" /> respectively. Only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/c/74c53cf1ee0e5e31d7791ca7394346930c8a03dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{27}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" /> is in the answer choices, so that would be our answer.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Sidenote\">Sidenote</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Sidenote\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that Bob's statement (that he knows who won/lost) comes after Alice tells him that she doesn't know who won. Since Alice doesn't know who won, Bob knows that she didn't get draw a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (or a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />), which tells him that his <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> must be lower than Alice's number. \n</p><p>~jd9\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Interstigation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/p9_RH4s-kBA?t=1524\">https://youtu.be/p9_RH4s-kBA?t=1524</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/vB3R4b-X3yA\">https://youtu.be/vB3R4b-X3yA</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by WhyMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/j-AZyR78-Ns\">https://youtu.be/j-AZyR78-Ns</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/RyN-fKNtd3A?t=1474\">https://youtu.be/RyN-fKNtd3A?t=1474</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B\">2021 Fall AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Pro